Mind preservation is a passive psionic ability that slows the aging
process through constant, unconscious mental discipline. The psionicist's
mind learns to maintain their body in a state of prolonged youth,
reducing the toll that time takes upon their physical form.

This power requires no activation and consumes no mana - it simply
becomes part of how the trained mind maintains the body. Once developed,
the ability works continuously, shielding the psionicist from a portion
of the ravages of time.

The effectiveness of mind preservation scales with the psionicist's
mastery of the technique. At full development, the power can reduce
apparent aging by up to one-fifth, allowing the psionicist to remain
vital and capable far longer than their peers.

Unlike many psionic abilities, mind preservation cannot be practiced or
improved through active use. It develops slowly through general mental
discipline and the overall advancement of psionic mastery. The mind
simply learns to preserve itself more effectively over time.

This subtle power is prized by those who walk the long paths of
adventure, for whom every additional year of vitality may mean the
difference between achieving their goals and succumbing to the march
of time.

